!Sample_submission_date = Jan 29 2019
!Sample_last_update_date = Aug 08 2019
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Mouse embryonic cells
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = developmental stage: Mid-gastrulation embryo (E7.0)
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tag: C57BL/6
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: Mouse embryonic cells
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Sample from sections were laser-microdissected and collected for single-cell based RNA sequencing.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Embryos from pre-gastrulation to late-gastrulation mouse were embedded with OCT and subjected to cryosection.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = According to Geo-seq (Chen et al., 2017), RNA from LCM samples were extracted by 5M GuSCN (Invitrogen, # 20012-043), then RNA was precipitated by ethanol with the help of RNA carrier.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Libraries were constructed using illumina Nextera XT DNA sample preparation kit
!Sample_description = processed data file: E7.0SingleCell.tpm.txt
!Sample_data_processing = The reads for all samples are mapped to the mm10 using Tophat v2.0.8b with parameter: -p 20 -g 1 -N 4 --read-edit-dist 4 --microexon-search
!Sample_data_processing = The mapped reads were used to estimate transcriptomic alignment rates, and were also used as input in Cufflinks v2.1.1 (Trapnell et al., 2013) to quantify gene expression levels (fragment per kilobase per million, FPKM) with the default parameters
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm10
